 listed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position to the end, and a page for each page holding a listed element; positions before the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first listed one cost nothing. An end is implausible when that span is more than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"16 × count + 64","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pages, where ","type":"text"},{"code":"count","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the number of vertices (or edges) listed: at most","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"16 page table entries per listed element (about 2 KB for a vertex, 256 bytes for an edge)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plus 64. So ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"vertexEnd\": 4611686018427387903","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with no vertices decodes, in O(1), while a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"payload cannot make decoding allocate without limit. A graph that has run more than that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"many empty pages past its live elements does not round-trip.","type":"text"}]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Decodes the format ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"encode(to:)"},{"text":" writes, every position and both ends restored. Throws","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DecodingError.dataCorrupted"},{"text":" for a positions\/values count mismatch, a repeated vertex,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"positions that do not strictly increase or that reach past their end, an odd-length edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"list, an endpoint out of range, or an implausible end.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/StableGraphs\/documentation\/StableGraphs\/StableDirectedGraph\/init(from:)"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/stablegr